# Class Booking — frontend environment
#
# Copy to frontend/.env.local (gitignored) for local overrides. Vite only
# exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to browser code — nothing else in
# process.env leaks into the built bundle.

# Leave unset. The API client (src/api/client.js) defaults to the page's own
# origin, calling `/api/...` there — Vercel's rewrites (vercel.json) proxy
# that to the Render backend server-side, and vite.config.js's dev-server
# proxy does the same locally against the backend on :3000. This is what
# keeps the auth cookie same-site (and therefore working) in both dev and
# production; see docs/decisions.md, Decision 51.
#
# Set this only to bypass the proxy and call a backend origin directly
# (cross-site) — doing so brings back the cross-site cookie problem the
# proxy exists to avoid, so it is not the default.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
